course: dictionary
lesson: 15860
title: Unfollowing accounts that upset you
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: On social media, you can unfollow a person or account so that you no longer see their posts. «Maya unfollowed the account because it kept posting mean jokes about her friends.» The words around unfollow tell you it is about posts and accounts, so it must mean stop following them.
explain: Unfollowing is a quiet choice. The other person is usually not told, but they may notice that their posts no longer show up for you. Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence: «Maya stopped following the account because it kept posting mean jokes.» It still makes sense, so you have the right meaning.
explain: You can unfollow an account that makes you feel bad, shows harmful content or upsets you. «If a page makes you feel scared or sad, you can unfollow it.» If something online worries you, you can also tell a trusted adult.
fact: Unfollow means to stop following a person or account on social media.
fact: When you unfollow someone, you no longer see their posts in your feed.
fact: You can unfollow an account that upsets you or shows harmful content.
fact: Unfollowing is usually not told to the other person, but they may notice.
fact: Unfollowing is a safe choice when something online makes you feel bad, and you can always tell a trusted adult too.
exercise: «Priya saw posts that made her feel bad, so she unfollowed the account.» What does unfollowed mean here? | Reported the account to the police | *Stopped following, so she no longer sees its posts | Sent a message to the account asking why | Shared all its posts with her friends
exercise: An account keeps showing you cruel pictures that make you feel upset. What is a safe thing to do? | Keep watching them to see if they get better | *Unfollow the account | Share the pictures with your friends | Post a cruel comment back
exercise: «Ella unfollowed her cousin's account.» Does her cousin get a message saying so? | *Usually not told, but they may notice | Yes, a loud alert is always sent | Yes, the police are told | Only if Ella blocks them
test: «Jay unfollowed the page because it shared unkind jokes.» What does unfollowed mean? | Liked every post on the page | *Stopped following the page, so he no longer sees its posts | Asked the page to make new posts | Copied the page's name
test: Which choice helps keep you safer online? | Reply with a rude comment | Share cruel posts with friends | *Unfollow an account that makes you feel bad | Keep reading posts that upset you
exam: Which sentence uses unfollow correctly? | Mia unfollows the account, so she unfollow it last week. | *Mia unfollowed the account that kept posting cruel pictures. | Mia unfollow the account yesterday. | Mia unfollowing the account is a picture.
